   1→/****************************************************************************
   2→ * dm_wifi.c — WiFi backend aligned with official Gemini-S1 / NuttX guide
   3→ *
   4→ * Official connect sequence (Gemini-S1 docs + 9.5 wifi_manager.c):
   5→ *   ifup wlan0
   6→ *   wapi mode wlan0 2          (WAPI_MODE_MANAGED / STA)
   7→ *   wapi psk wlan0 <pass> 3 2  (3 = WPA_ALG_CCMP, 2 = WPA2)
   8→ *   wapi essid wlan0 <ssid> 1  (1 = WAPI_ESSID_ON)
   9→ *   renew wlan0
  10→ *
  11→ * Fixes applied:
  12→ *   1. Do not write s_cur_ssid when DHCP fails (!got_ip); dm_wifi_connected()
  13→ *      checks both s_cur_ssid and s_cur_ip so failed auto-connect never fakes
  14→ *      "Connected" state.
  15→ *   2. Manual scan/connect sets s_manual_override = 1, immediately interrupting
  16→ *      background boot auto-connect so clicking "Scan" is never blocked by
  17→ *      s_conn_busy.
  18→ *   3. Robust wapi scan parser: skips non-MAC header/log lines, preserves SSIDs
  19→ *      containing spaces, deduplicates BSSIDs, and sorts by RSSI descending.
  20→ *   4. Avoids double DHCP calls in the same loop iteration.
  21→ *   5. Credentials are saved only AFTER an IP was obtained and the requested
  22→ *      ESSID verified (a wrong password no longer poisons boot auto-connect).
  23→ *   6. Previous association/key is dropped before each attempt, and open APs
  24→ *      explicitly clear any leftover WPA key (alg NONE).
  25→ *   7. wapi command return codes are checked (psk/essid); FlowDesk saves
  26→ *      verified credentials to its own /data files, avoiding a second
  27→ *      WAPI/NSH startup owner.
  28→ *   8. Hardcoded fallback SSID/password removed from source.
  29→ *   9. Boot and link-loss auto-connect use only verified credentials from
  30→ *      FlowDesk /data files or the existing WAPI JSON config; no SSID/PSK is
  31→ *      compiled into the application.
  32→ *  10. Ported from 9.5 wifi_manager.c: the connect sequence retries up to
  33→ *      DM_WIFI_CONN_ROUNDS with a 5s gap, and uses "wapi show" (AP all-zero)
  34→ *      as an extra association check in addition to the IPv4 check.
  35→ ****************************************************************************/
  36→
